Package: keel-web
Architecture: all
Depends:
 anubis (>= 1.27.0-0+keel3),
 keel (>= 0.15.0),
 keel-core,
 keel-overlay-anubis,
 keel-overlay-coraza (>= 0.1.2),
 keel-overlay-nginx,
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: Keel Web, the base of every Keel web appliance
 The appliance manifest of Keel Web (handbook decisions 0030 and 0041),
 installed as /usr/share/keel/appliances/web.yaml: Keel Core plus the
 nginx, coraza and anubis overlays, Nginx alone in a simple installation
 and the three of them in the cloud modes.
 .
 It also ships the default site of a simple installation,
 /etc/nginx/sites-available/keel-default (HTTP and HTTPS with the machine's
 certificate, a placeholder page until a site is configured, its own 404
 and 50x pages), which its postinst enables in place of Debian's default
 site; its Anubis front, /etc/nginx/sites-available/default-anubis (HTTPS
 with the machine's certificate, port 80 redirecting to it); and the state
 hook that keel spec apply runs when the anubis overlay is turned on or
 off, which puts the front in the default site's place and back. Coraza and
 Anubis are enabled by keel from the instance spec, never by this package.
